WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
(curious music)

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.733
- [Narrator] These images

00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:04.440
show Russia's Black Sea
Fleet headquarters in Crimea

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.953
before and after an
attack on September 22nd.

00:00:09.026 --> 00:00:10.200
(explosion booms)

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.270
The strike killed and injured dozens

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.340
including senior leaders of the Navy,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.474
according to Kyiv.

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:16.440
(explosion booms)

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.050
Another attack on Russia's
principal dry dock

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.780
in the city of Sevastopol in mid-September

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.030
destroyed a large landing ship

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.040
and heavily damaged a submarine.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.950
- Ukraine has shown that it's
not only on the receiving end,

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.890
it can attack Russia in return.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.530
- [Narrator] The assaults are
part of a Ukrainian strategy

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.470
to weaken military and
logistics facilities

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.240
on the occupied peninsula.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.880
- Ukraine wants to cut off Crimea

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.730
to make the peninsula untenable.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.130
- [Narrator] Here's why Ukraine
has ramped up its attacks

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.759
on the peninsula.

00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:49.592
(tense music)

00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:53.580
Crimea is crucial for Russia's
operations in Ukraine.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.800
It's a supply hub for Russian forces

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.260
resisting Ukraine's counter offensive

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.990
which started in summer 2023.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.340
- Most important fighting

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.680
is happening in the southeast of Ukraine.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.550
Russian troops there are
being supplied from Crimea,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.160
so that's incredibly
important in particular

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.520
because the supply from
the east is not as strong.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.590
- [Narrator] Russia has
also turned the peninsula

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.480
into a heavily militarized zone

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.940
since the annexation in 2014.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.390
Sevastopol is the home of
Russia's Black Sea Fleet,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.120
where some of the country's
most sophisticated warships

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.953
are stationed.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:30.000
(missile whooshing)

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.370
- One way that Black
Sea Fleet has been used

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.250
as a way to launch cruise
missiles that have struck military

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.120
and civilian infrastructure
targets within Ukraine.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.380
- [Narrator] There are also several

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.330
important military air bases,

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.750
some of which Ukraine has
targeted since last year

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.250
To protect its assets,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.470
Russia has stationed
their air defense systems

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.270
across the peninsula.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.430
In September, Ukraine said it destroyed

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.690
a sophisticated air defense
system known as the S-400.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:00.600
- The Ukrainians say
that they sent in drones

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.265
to attack the S-400's radars.

00:02:04.265 --> 00:02:05.280
(explosives crackling)

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.110
They used two Neptune missiles

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.730
that were made by the Ukrainians

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.400
and that they destroyed this S-400 system.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.380
- [Narrator] Ukraine
has intensified attacks

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.720
on the occupied peninsula in recent months

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.690
as its ability to target Crimea improved.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.600
- Ukraine has gotten cruise missiles

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.700
from Britain and France.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.610
They've also developed their own weapons

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.870
that they've been able to use,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.000
drones, torpedoes,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.250
and the Ukrainians have figured out

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.670
how to orchestrate very
complicated attacks.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.860
- [Narrator] Russia acknowledged
that two of its warships

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.570
had been struck in Sevastopol

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.490
and one service member was missing

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.830
after the attack on the Navy headquarters,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.313
but it didn't confirm any damage
to its air defense systems.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.220
As winter approaches,

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.800
Kyiv is trying to neutralize the threats

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.590
that Russia's military
assets in Crimea posed

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.590
to Ukraine's critical infrastructure.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.490
- Ukraine would like

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.800
not only to continue
these attacks on Crimea

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.020
but also to ramp them up.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.280
A key part of that is
about getting supplies

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.320
of more long range missiles

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.350
and longer range missiles from the west.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.180
The numbers of cruise missiles

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.450
from the UK and from France are limited.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.470
They're producing their own
Neptune cruise missiles,

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.880
but it's not clear

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.340
how many of those they're able to produce.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.980
- [Narrator] In September,
the White House told Ukraine

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.790
it would send advanced long
range surface-to-air missiles,

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.276
according to US officials.

00:03:35.276 --> 00:03:36.750
(missile whooshes)

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.780
The new missiles would add to
Ukraine's ability to launch

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.580
longer range strikes,

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.970
turning Crimea into an
even more dangerous place

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.383
for Russian troops.

